NAME:     tail - end-of-file printerAUTHOR:     Eric Williams  WD6CMU  [71336,1424]SYSTEM CONFIGURATION:     OS9/68K v2.1, MW C v2.2SYNTAX:     tail [<file>]DESCRIPTION:     tail copies the last (up to 24) lines of the input data stream tostandard output.  If no file name is provided, standard input is used. If the input stream is a RBF-type device, a seek to the end of file isused, otherwise lines of text are read and discarded to reach the end ofthe file.  In this manner, tail may be used to process data piped to itfrom another program. BUGS:     Hangs on zero-length files.